-- title:
--   Relations generated in degree ≤ 1 from a hyperplane section
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $n, m, g$ be natural numbers, write $S = K[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ for the polynomial ring $\mathtt{MvPolynomial (Fin (n+1)) } K$, and let $F : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to S$ be a family with each $F_i$ homogeneous of degree $m$; let $\ell \in S$ be homogeneous of degree $1$, and put $I = (\,\mathrm{range}\,F\,)$ for the ideal generated by the $F_i$. Two hypotheses are imposed. First, a colon condition in degree $m$: every $f \in S$ homogeneous of degree $m$ with $\ell f \in I$ already lies in $I$. Second, a presentation of the relations modulo $\ell$: for every $d$ and every family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to S$ with all $c_i$ homogeneous of degree $d$ and $\sum_i c_i F_i \in (\ell)$, the vector $c$ lies in the $S$-submodule of $S^g$ spanned by those vectors $l$ for which there is some $d' \le 1$ with all $l_i$ homogeneous of degree $d'$ and $\sum_i l_i F_i \in (\ell)$. The conclusion: for every $d$ and every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,g \to S$ with all $c_i$ homogeneous of degree $d$ and $\sum_i c_i F_i = 0$, the vector $c$ lies in the $S$-submodule of $S^g$ spanned by those $l$ for which there is some $d' \le 1$ with all $l_i$ homogeneous of degree $d'$ and $\sum_i l_i F_i = 0$.
--
--   This is the $\mathrm{Tor}_1$ case of the principle by which bounds on the degrees of syzygies descend from a hyperplane section: a linear presentation of the image of $I$ in $S/(\ell)$, together with equality of $(I:\ell)$ and $I$ in degree $m$, forces the syzygy module of $F_1,\dots,F_g$ itself to be generated in degrees at most $1$. It is used in the proof of [`MvPolynomial.exists_forall_eval_ne_zero_mem_of_mul_mem_of_finrank_piece_succ_eq_macaulayPow`](thm.html#MvPolynomial.exists_forall_eval_ne_zero_mem_of_mul_mem_of_finrank_piece_succ_eq_macaulayPow).
